      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Dear Stakeholders,\n\nVertical scaling, also known as scaling up, involves increasing the power of a single machine, such as adding more RAM, CPU, or storage. In contrast, horizontal scaling, or scaling out, involves adding more machines or servers to distribute the workload evenly across a larger pool of resources. Vertical scaling can be quicker to implement but is limited by the physical capacities of individual machines, while horizontal scaling offers better flexibility and resilience but may require more complex configurations and management. Both approaches aim to enhance our system's performance and ensure reliability during our infrastructure changes.",
